<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer orders drop, but positive outlook.</title>
<headline>Sulzer orders drop, but positive outlook.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sulzer Technology Corp. said 1996 group orders fell three percent to 5.5 billion Swiss francs and it confirmed that net profit will be seriously affected by restructuring charges and extraordinary expenses.</p>
<p>Sulzer, however, said in a statement that its outlook for 1997 was positive.</p>
<p>Sulzer also said that it would adopt International Accounting Standards (IAS) in its 1996 accounts, which includes a revaluation of land and buildings according to the standard of acquisition values.</p>
</text>
